                <pb facs="0453" n="335" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg335"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00 Nanking/247: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-31T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 31,
                                1928—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>For the Minister. Department’s March 31, 1 p.m., your March 31, 8 p.m. Notes
                    which you have signed are satisfactory. Department has no further comments to
                    make.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
